From 3ddf3ed8c4e42e087d5612e054242db17a715526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 20:11:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rzv2n: xspi_setup: settle SPI flash before memory-map reads

After xspi_reset() + xspi_read_identification() complete, the SPI flash
is responsive to manual commands but has not finished entering memory-
mapped read mode. The XSPI controller's BMCTL0 path is up, but the chip
itself needs at least tRPH (~32 us per IS25WP032D datasheet) plus a
mode-latch window before XIP reads return real data instead of zeros.

BL2 does not respect that window: rz_io_setup() calls xspi_setup() and
the very next consumer (fip_dev_init) issues a memmap read at
RZV2N_SPIROM_FIP_BASE. The first 16 bytes come back zero, fip_file_open
treats TOC entry 0's all-zero UUID as the null terminator, and returns
-ENOENT. BL2 prints 'Failed to load image id 3 (-2)' and panics.

The race is masked at LOG_LEVEL=50 because the INFO()/VERBOSE() prints
between DDR init and FIP load clock out ~4 ms of UART traffic at 115200
baud, providing enough incidental settling time. Bit-identical builds
at LOG_LEVEL=20 reliably hit the failure.

Add a 10 ms mdelay after xspi_setup completes its init+probe sequence.
This is far longer than the chip-spec'd tRPH but guarantees deterministic
behavior across LOG_LEVEL settings and is invisible at boot scale.

Signed-off-by: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
---
 plat/renesas/rz/common/drivers/xspi.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/renesas/rz/common/drivers/xspi.c b/plat/renesas/rz/common/drivers/xspi.c
index 9340f9838..ea3fa52b9 100644
--- a/plat/renesas/rz/common/drivers/xspi.c
+++ b/plat/renesas/rz/common/drivers/xspi.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <stdint.h>
+#include <drivers/delay_timer.h>
 #include <lib/utils_def.h>
 #include <lib/mmio.h>
 #include <arch_helpers.h>
@@ -247,5 +248,16 @@ int xspi_setup(void)
 	if (ret == XSPI_SUCCESS)
 		ret = xspi_read_identification();
 
+	/*
+	 * Allow the SPI flash to fully settle into memory-mapped read mode after
+	 * RESET + RDID before any consumer issues an XIP read. Without this,
+	 * BL2's FIP TOC walk at the SPI XIP base races the chip and reads zeros,
+	 * causing fip_file_open() to hit an all-zero UUID at TOC entry 0
+	 * (mistaken for the null terminator) and return -ENOENT for BL31. The
+	 * datasheet tRPH for IS25WP032D is ~32 us; 10 ms is conservative and
+	 * dwarfed by overall boot time.
+	 */
+	mdelay(10);
+
 	return ret;
 }
